        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8b34a110-098c-5137-82f9-2fd3ef360dfe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Young, Guy Pearce, Jeremy Irons, Orlando Jones, Samantha Mumba, Mark Addy, Sienna Guillory, Phyllida Law, Charles Dickens\n- Works: The Alan Young Show, Mickey's Christmas Carol, The Time Machine (2002 film), The Time Machine (1960 film), A Christmas Carol\n- Organizations: Disney, TV Guide, Emmy Awards, Academy Awards\n- Roles: actor, voice actor, comedian, radio host, television host\n\nFacts:\n- Alan Young, born Angus Young on November 19, 1919, was a British-born Canadian-American actor, voice actor, comedian, and radio and television host.\n- During the 1940s and 1950s, Alan Young starred in his radio and television variety and comedy program The Alan Young Show.\n- In 1951, the television version of The Alan Young Show earned Alan Young two Emmy Awards.\n- TV Guide called Alan Young \"The Charlie Chaplin of Television.\"\n- In 1960, Alan Young appeared in the film adaptation The Time Machine.\n- Mickey's Christmas Carol is an adaptation of Charles Dickens's A Christmas Carol and casts Scrooge McDuck as Ebenezer Scrooge.\n- In 1983, Alan Young first voiced Disney's Scrooge McDuck in the Academy Award-nominated short film Mickey's Christmas Carol.\n- Alan Young continued voicing Scrooge McDuck in other films, television series, and video games for more than thirty years until his death on May 19, 2016.\n- The Time Machine (2002 film) stars Guy Pearce, Jeremy Irons, Orlando Jones, Samantha Mumba, Mark Addy, Sienna Guillory, and Phyllida Law.\n- The Time Machine (2002 film) includes a cameo by Alan Young.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4e3c3536-25b6-56b5-a4ae-02e245f86965",
        "text": "Page: Alan Young. Sentence: Alan Young (born Angus Young; November 19, 1919 – May 19, 2016) was a British-born Canadian-American actor, voice actor, comedian and radio and television host/personality who \"TV Guide\" called \"The Charlie Chaplin of Television\".\nPage: Alan Young. Sentence: Young was also the voice of Disney's Scrooge McDuck for over thirty years, first in the Academy Award-nominated short film \"Mickey's Christmas Carol\" (1983) and in various other films, TV series and video games until his death.\nPage: Alan Young. Sentence: During the 1940s and 1950s, he starred in his own variety/comedy sketch shows \"The Alan Young Show\" on radio and television, the latter gaining him two Emmy Awards in 1951.\nPage: Mickey's Christmas Carol. Sentence: The cartoon is an adaptation of Charles Dickens' \"A Christmas Carol\", starring Scrooge McDuck as Ebenezer Scrooge.\nPage: The Time Machine (2002 film). Sentence: The film stars Guy Pearce, Jeremy Irons, Orlando Jones, Samantha Mumba, Mark Addy, Sienna Guillory and Phyllida Law, and includes a cameo by Alan Young, who also appeared in the 1960 film adaptation.",
